    "prompt": "Use attached sprite atlas only as CHARACTER IDENTITY and painted 2D style reference. Create a NEW complete upgraded creature action atlas: Pressure Colossus, the stronger upgrade of the same gigantic LIVING Zaun chemtech-augmented human. Preserve clearly organic bald human head and huge exposed muscular chest/upper arms/thighs. Upgrade visibly stronger: broader powerful musculature, larger reinforced striking cuffs, bronze shoulder guards that leave chest and arms visible, reinforced leather harness, heavier plum waistcloth, three protected chemical-green pressure bottles at upper back and thicker piston braces along lower legs. A visible painted Zaun respirator-mask regional crest on the plum belt tab and a bronze cuff (angular mask with narrow eyes and twin round cheek filters). Not fully metal, not robotic, no champion copy, no wings, no floating badge. Hand-painted original Heroes III 1999 compact sprite style, same battle camera facing right, upper-left light, texture and restrained highlights. Use true transparent background, opaque body, soft contact shadows only under grounded poses. Every cell a different coherent real anatomical pose.\n\nEXACT 6 COLUMNS x 8 ROWS, tall portrait atlas, equal 256-square cells, desired1536x2048. Every cell one COMPLETE isolated full-body sprite with generous 30px transparent margins, no neighbor contact, common body scale about190px tall; baseline foot y220. Atlas reads left-to-right:\nRow1: six AIRBORNE forward leap travel phases, knees alternately tucked and extended, both feet off ground, torso braced, powerful athletic leap. No walking or standing phase in this row, no wings or boosters.\nRow2 col1-4: four quiet ready/alert breathing poses on ground. col5 neutral standing HOLD pose. col6 independent full-body portrait standing, feet grounded.\nRow3 col1-4: four impact/recoil phases then recovery. col5 independent right-facing small-map stance. col6 independent left-facing lunging encounter attack.\nRow4 col1-4: four TURN phases starting normal right-facing, rotating chest/head toward camera stepwise until front-facing. col5 independent right-facing encounter punch. col6 standing portrait.\nRow5 col1-4: four DEFEND phases forearms lifted to block chest, absorb hit, return. col5-6 quiet stance variants.\nRow6: six DEATH phases stagger, kneel, fall, ground impact, settle, final horizontal corpse.\nRow7 col1-4: four grounded LAUNCH phases, deep crouch compressing knees, weight driving upward, toes release, initial rising airborne. col5-6 spare grounded stance variants.\nRow8 col1-4: four LANDING phases descending feet extended, feet contact, deep knee impact absorption, regain neutral standing. col5-6 spare grounded stance variants.\n\nAvoid text, grid lines, labels, scenery, tiny body at top, crops, body crossing cells, glossy3D, vector or cartoon. This is actual painted animation art, not duplicate cutouts. Same character/equipment throughout and stronger than reference base.\n",
